          "body": "A **seventh chord** is a triad plus the note a 7th above the root. The main types:\n\n| Symbol | Name | Build | From C |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Cmaj7 | major seventh | major triad + major 7th | C E G B |\n| C7 | dominant seventh | major triad + minor 7th | C E G B♭ |\n| Cm7 | minor seventh | minor triad + minor 7th | C E♭ G B♭ |\n| Cm7♭5 | half-diminished | diminished triad + minor 7th | C E♭ G♭ B♭ |\n| Cdim7 | diminished seventh | diminished triad + diminished 7th | C E♭ G♭ B♭♭ (sounds as A) |\n\nRight-hand root-position fingering: **1 2 3 5**.",
